# Read by engine/__init__.py at import, from this directory only. Copy to .env
# (gitignored) and fill in. A variable already set in the shell wins.

# The recovery agent's LLM planner. Without a key it uses the rule planner and
# every number stays reproducible, which is why the demo does not need this.
# Get one at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey. Do not judge a key by its
# shape: this file used to claim real keys are 39 characters starting "AIza",
# and a working 52-character "AQ.Ab8R..." key was written off on that basis for
# a day. There is one test that matters, and it takes five seconds:
#   python -m agents.recovery
GEMINI_API_KEY=
GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash

# Which ledger the API serves. Leave it commented out. Unset, the server picks
# the newest non-empty database in data/ by itself and logs which one it chose;
# setting it turns that off. data/checkpost.db is the one file that is reliably
# empty, so copying this file with the line live is exactly how you get a blank
# dashboard with nothing on screen saying why. Uncomment only to pin one run.
# CHECKPOST_DB=data/replay.db

# Razorpay test mode only. Never a live key. Nothing reads these yet — no real
# money moves in this project.
RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=
RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET=
